 that receipt is retained at
 [`qualification/dsv4/collectives/tp4_tree_bitwise_20260814/result.json`](qualification/dsv4/collectives/tp4_tree_bitwise_20260814/result.json).
 
+### Reusable 130-step TP4 decode program
+
+An unmerged candidate based on `main@da7f910` replaces the per-collective
+submit/callback control path with one caller-owned, preallocated program and a
+producer/consumer CUDA graph pair. The terminal callback is published only
+after all 130 operations release their transport resources and both graphs
+publish their drained state. Rearm performs no allocation, graph recapture,
+node patch, or host payload copy.
+
+The runtime and serving configurations now fail closed on exactly two graph
+executables per pipeline slot. The obsolete `3 * layer_count + 1` graph-island
+contract and its 130/34/31 configuration values are removed; the per-step
+collective algorithm still comes from the normal payload-size catalog rather
+than a B1-only driver or compatibility path.
+
+The isolated four-GB10 test used the paired direct rail plus switched rail,
+8 KiB exact BF16 reductions, two credits, and the catalog-selected direct
+all-to-all algorithm. Three independent one-launch runs measured rank means of
+36.8725, 36.9555, and 36.3815 us/collective: **36.7365 us mean**, or
+4.7757 ms for the 130-step device interval. Three second launches of the same
+graph executables after zero-allocation rearm measured 28.4880, 36.2605, and
+32.7478 us/collective: **32.4988 us mean**, or 4.2248 ms for 130 steps. The
+spread is retained rather than presenting the fastest run as the result.
+
+All 24 rank receipts returned status zero, the exact value 10.0, zero BF16
+mismatches, hash `22b433e29b34c383`, and exactly one terminal callback per
+launch. The mixed program also has host-unit coverage for a terminal U64-max
+step and failure after 0, 1, 2, and 5 submitted steps. A GB10 CUDA test passed
+bit-exact producer mirroring and TP4 U64 max. A transport-operation failure
+also drains without the consumer result signal, proving cancellation unblocks
+both graphs before the sole terminal callback. The standard B1 module smoke
+validator passed on the GA stage-8 slice. This is isolated collective evidence,
+not an end-to-end decode throughput result or merged-main qualification.
+
+Raw run receipts and artifact hashes are retained in
+[`tp4-rolling-program-terminal-drain-summary.json`](qualification/dsv4/performance/tp4_b1_20260814/tp4-rolling-program-terminal-drain-summary.json).
+
